# Plugin UI

- Entries: `docs/agent/registry.md` `## Plugin UI`. Couplings: `docs/agent/seams.md`
  `## Plugin UI and runtime`. The plugin-facing contract is the `plugin-api` rule.
- `PluginTabViewModel.kt` is very large: find members with `rg -n` and Read by
  offset. Up to three instances per plugin exist (Library, reader card, Settings).
- Position writes go through `ProgressWriter`, with the catalog row created first; never write a
  plugin position table directly.
- Build book ids with `PluginManager.bookIdFor`; never write a plugin id or a `rr:`/`pt:` prefix as a
  literal in app code.
- Story actions are `MediaCardModel` content from `PluginMediaCardAdapter`; the reader reuses the same
  overlays, so hide actions it cannot do through `ReaderHiddenActions`.
- Sign-in is the site's own page in a WebView; the plugin never sees a password. Cookie handling is
  process-wide (`CookieManager`).
- Sync, erase and update code share `TwoWaySync.lock`; see the `sync` rule.
- History: `../flow-reader-chats/areas/plugins.md`.
